{
  "name": "Provision client onboarding in Google Drive, ClickUp and Slack (demo)",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "f7e8ddf6-8862-47b8-9a79-3e89a279a507",
      "name": "Overview and Setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -3248,
        16
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 512,
        "height": 880,
        "content": "> **Demonstration workflow. Not for production use without changes.**\n> Running it again for the same client creates duplicate folders, lists and tasks: it has no reuse or duplicate checks, and the AI chooses the due dates instead of computing them. It also creates a public Slack channel and emails the client automatically. Add duplicate protection, review the AI plan before tasks are created, and test with your own sample client first.\n\n## Provision client onboarding workspaces\n\nTurn one internal form submission and proposal PDF into a ready-to-use onboarding workspace. The workflow extracts the proposal, creates and shares a Google Drive folder, creates a ClickUp folder and list, uses OpenAI to produce a structured task plan, posts an internal Slack handoff, and emails the client their Drive access.\n\n### How it works\n\n1. Collect client details and the signed proposal.\n2. Create the Drive and ClickUp workspace.\n3. Generate and create onboarding tasks.\n4. Notify the delivery team and welcome the client.\n\n### Required setup\n\n- [ ] Connect Basic Auth, Google Drive, ClickUp, OpenAI, Slack, and Gmail credentials; reuse each credential on matching nodes.\n- [ ] Select the Drive and parent folder in **Create Main Client Folder**.\n- [ ] Select the ClickUp workspace and space in **Create ClickUp Client Folder**.\n- [ ] Test with a sample PDF before activation.\n\n### Optional variables\n\nIn **Configure Onboarding Workspace**: `scheduling_url` adds a booking call-to-action when present; `account_manager_name` defaults to \u201cAccount manager\u201d; `agency_name` defaults to \u201cYour team.\u201d You may also change the Drive sharing role and workflow timezone. Never paste secrets into Edit Fields.\n\n### Customization tips\n\nAdjust the AI instructions and message copy for your process. Each run creates new objects (there are no reuse checks), so reconcile completed steps before rerunning after a partial failure."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
